                <pb facs="0273" n="267" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg267"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 14.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. de Cologan to Mr. L. C. Hopkins, His Britannic
                        Majesty’s consul-general and senior consul at Tientsin.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic">July 3,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Consul-General</hi>: I have the honor to inform
                    you that the diplomatic corps has approved the proposal contained in your letter
                    of the 20th of June last, to double the taxes already existing for the
                    improvement of the navigation of the Peiho.</p>
                <p>Please accept, Mr. Consul-General, the expression of my distinguished
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">B. J. de Cologan.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
